<title>USA: BPA LOWERS TUES PEAK FIRM POWER BY $1/MWH.</title>
<headline>BPA LOWERS TUES PEAK FIRM POWER BY $1/MWH.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) continued to offer 200 megawatts of peak, firm power for next-day delivery, but lowered prices by $1.00 per megawatt hour (MWh), the agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>For Wednesday, the Portland, Oregon-based federal power marketing agency offered Northwest sales at $20.00 per megawatt hour (MWh) and California-Oregon border deliveries at $22.00.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 955 6761))</p>
